            <ArticleTitle>Repair of the defect in spondylolysis or minimal degrees of spondylolisthesis by segmental wire fixation and bone grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>673-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Twenty-two patients with spondylolysis and minimal degrees of spondylolisthesis have been treated with repair of the defect by segmental wire fixation and bone grafting. Twenty-one patients are available for follow-up. Eighty percent of the patients obtained good to excellent results, and 90% obtained solid fusion of the pars defect. The technique would appear to have the greatest use in patients less than 30 years of age with minimal degrees of displacement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
